Z||000000||superXmotorsports||11-29-1999||11:14 PM||||I'm not sure what replacement bulbs are available for Fiero's, but I ordered $100 worth of 'super' bulbs for my Spyder last week.  That same night a read a comparison test on a website that most aftermarket bulbs didn't live up to the advertisement (they performed tests, etc)  Today my bulbs arrived:  PIAA Super White 9006's (lowbeam), Heliolight gold 9005's (highbeam), and Eurolight H3 100w neon blue (driving lights).<BR>Since I used 3 different brands I can honestly say these are more hype than light.  The neon blue driving lights are just slightly briter white than std (I was going just for cosmetics on those) (and they took about 1 1/2hrs to install)  The 'gold' 100w highbeams only look gold when turned off and you look at the reflection in the housing!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The PIAA's look just like stock too.<BR>(by the way I did check 1 at a time to compare)<P>Anyway just my life experience for someone to hopefully benefit by!||||reg||4
